# r1113 chunk 4, boot B: ONE boot, group B fresh normal world (seed 8675309, structures on), level r1113c4b.
# Rows: SQ-NSM-08 (new world on the moved Worldgen / Calendar namespaces), SQ-GAP-03 (Bushier Flowers worldgen off),
# SQ-RD-10 (part of SQ-RDB-03: savanna village farm crops on the baked Rustic member).
# SQ-GAP is marked HOLD in the queue (after the Common suite): the condition is met (SQ-CGE 2026-11-08, nothing open);
# skip SQ-GAP-03 with --rows if the orchestrator keeps the hold.
#
# Setup (OUT = scratch dir, srv = OUT/srv, INST = instance root):
#   bash $INST/tools/scratch_query/prep_srv.sh OUT r1113c4b B spawn-animals=true
#   python3 $INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py toml srv/config/loadingprotection-common.toml '"Loading Protection Configuration"' protectionDuration 1
#   no srv config edits otherwise (SQ-NSM-08 wants the live creativeworldgen-common.toml as shipped)
#   probes: zz_zq_probe.js from prep_srv.sh only.
# Same boot afterwards: rerun_b.qb (SQ-HH-328, needs hh_mw_probe.js as zz_hh_mw_probe.js; it wants the Async Locator
#   free, so run it BEFORE this batch's locate rows: qrun rerun_b.qb first, then c4_b.qb).
# Id fixes: the queue's `[creativedelight] village farm crops added to 5 farm processor lists` line is now
#   "added to N pool elements" (VillageFarmCrops.java); structure tags are #creativeworldgen:meta/* and group/* (the
#   kubejs/exported structure dumps still show creativeengineering: names from before the 11-10 move).
pace 2

## SQ-NSM-08a | new world boots on the moved namespaces: no structure or dimension errors, summaries clean
bootexpect Done \(
bootreject (?i)Unknown structure start|Found reference to unknown structure|Unknown structure piece id
bootreject (?i)WorldGenSettings.*(error|failed)
bootreject (?i)creativeengineering:(yellowstone|hub|autumnsky|springsky|summersky|wintersky|desert|shield|flowergrove|flowerhills|flowerridge)
shell grep -nE "\[mob-spawns\]|\[mob_spawns\]|\[bee-nests\]|\[bee_nests\]" logs/latest.log | cut -c1-260 | head -20; echo "idle mentions: $(grep -E '\[(mob-spawns|mob_spawns|bee-nests|bee_nests)\]' logs/latest.log | grep -ci idle)"
look mob-spawns and bee-nests summaries present, no rule idle (shell output)

## SQ-RD-10 | savanna village farms carry Rustic crops (log line and a census of one village)
bootexpect \[creativedelight\] village farm crops added to \d+
> locate structure minecraft:village_savanna
waitlog (?:The nearest minecraft:village_savanna is at|Could not find) 300
capture SV The nearest minecraft:village_savanna is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
> chunky world minecraft:overworld
> chunky shape square
> chunky center {SV1} {SV3}
> chunky radius 96
> chunky start
waitlog Task finished 900
> save-all flush
waitlog Saved the game 120
shell python3 $INST/tools/scratch_query/region_blocks.py blocks r1113c4b 'rusticdelight:(cotton|bell_pepper|coffee)' --box $(( {SV1} - 96 )) $(( {SV3} - 96 )) $(( {SV1} + 96 )) $(( {SV3} + 96 )) 2>&1 | tail -25
look some savanna farm crops are Rustic cotton (counts in the shell output); plains farms unchanged is not checked here

